  "vulnerabilities": [
    {
      "type": "flash_loan / flash_mint governance bypass (proposal spam / unauthorized proposal creation)",
      "severity": "high",
      "vulnerable_function": "isGranted",
      "location": "MinVotingPowerCondition.isGranted",
      "explanation": "The permission check uses `token.balanceOf(_who) + lockManager.getLockedBalance(_who)` to determine whether `_who` meets `plugin.minProposerVotingPower()`. If the governance token supports flashloans/flashminting (or can be temporarily acquired via any atomic mechanism), an attacker can temporarily inflate `token.balanceOf(_who)` within a single transaction to pass `isGranted()` without having any enduring stake. This breaks the intended anti-spam / economic-security gate for proposal creation, allowing untrusted users to create proposals with effectively zero lasting voting power. Because `isGranted()` is a view and does not enforce any lock duration or snapshot, the check is trivially satisfied by transient balances.",
      "attack_scenario": "1) Attacker takes a flashloan/flashmint of the governance token to their EOA/contract.\n2) Within the same transaction, calls the governance plugin function gated by this condition to create proposals (the permission check passes due to the temporary `balanceOf`).\n3) Optionally lock/vote and trigger early execution if the broader system allows it, using the temporary tokens.\n4) Repay the flashloan before transaction end.\n5) Repeat to spam proposals and/or execute actions if other governance parameters permit.",
      "suggested_fix": "Do not count free token balance for proposer eligibility. Use only non-transferable/locked voting power (or a prior snapshot):\n- Replace `token.balanceOf(_who) + lockManager.getLockedBalance(_who)` with `lockManager.getLockedBalance(_who)`.\n- Additionally, record proposal creator and enforce that the required locked amount remains locked until proposal expiration/execution (or use snapshot-based voting power at a prior block)."
    }
  ],
  "overall_explanation": "The contract’s only security-relevant logic is `isGranted()`, which authorizes proposal creation based on current token balance plus locked balance. Using live `balanceOf` makes the threshold bypassable via flashloan/flashmint or other transient acquisition, enabling proposal-gating circumvention and governance spam (and potentially execution depending on external plugin rules). Restrict eligibility to locked/snapshotted voting power and/or enforce lock duration tied to proposals."
}
